{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done","id":1077105,"title":"I'm Done","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-12T11:52:03-07:00","id":1077105,"title":"I'm Done","content":"I can no longer comfortably support Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> I've enjoyed these games for years, consider many of them near and dear to my heart, and for a while really hoped to be picked up as a freelancer, but from here on out I'm no longer touching WoD, CofD, or anything else they put out; I'll receive whatever's coming from Kickstarters I've already funded, and that's it. I might come back to playing Mummy or Promethean with my gaming group at some point in the future, but for right now everything is so tainted that I'm pretty damn close to just walking away and playing other things. <br /> <br /> The entire situation with new White Wolf (not only the actions of Martin and Zak, but how threads rightly objecting to those actions on this forum were locked and deleted) pushed me pretty close to the edge, but what's got me finally upset enough to walk away has been everything recently with David Hill. To have the Changeling 2e developer so quickly disavowed by his former peers has been incredibly hard to see, and the prospect of the game he's been previewing for literally years now no longer being the game we'll be getting, in favor of largely new and chopped up content and minimized credit due to him (and according to some, lessened pay), is honestly disgusting. He's done good work, and deserves better than this.<br /> <br /> So I'm done. I'm not going to be buying any further Onyx Path content, and I'm probably not going to be playing much more of it either. It's been nice interacting with some of you, and I've got pleasant memories.<br /> <br /> This thread will probably get locked or deleted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:16:18-07:00","id":1077116,"title":"","content":"I feel similarly. When there are at least 3 freelancers sharing stories about abysmally low pay (less than minimum wage), missed pay, and docked pay, it's hard to justify buying these products. At best, it curbs my (considerable) enthusiasm for these wonderful worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:17:01-07:00","id":1077118,"title":"","content":"I mean, the whole Zak &amp; Martin are things that people are upset with, but I don't know enough about the Changeling 2E situation, I'm just looking forward to its release. I think Onyx Path for the most part has tried their best to publish content that is engaging and stay on the side of caution with everything that has gone on, but I respect your opinion. Sorry you've gotten to the point of not supporting Onyx Path, but it's always sad to see people leave <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Best of luck Lex, in future gaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:22:33-07:00","id":1077122,"title":"","content":"That's...sad new. I was always more of a lurker than anything and we never really interacted much, but you were always someone whose posts and comments I found interesting, well-written and a whole lot of other positive adjectives. I looked forward both to your replies and your works. I do understand your position though and i would not dare to try to make you change your mind.<br /> <br /> I wish you the best, Lex","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:23:21-07:00","id":1077124,"title":"","content":"From how they've treated David and my buddy Holden and the handling of the Zak dealio... I mean I can't say i won't ever buy another Onyx Path book, but damn if that's not a tempting arrangement right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:26:36-07:00","id":1077126,"title":"","content":"Looks like it may just be GURPS and Shadowrun for me, at least until OPP/white wolf gets it's act together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:31:34-07:00","id":1077130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077126#post1077126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like it may just be GURPS and Shadowrun for me, at least until OPP/white wolf gets it's act together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to distract from this thread, but Shadowrun treats their freelancers pretty fucking awfully; there was a whole embezzling scandal that was never resolved, and the situation with pay was so bad that the Eclipse Phase people bought their own rights back from the main company in order to go independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:37:36-07:00","id":1077136,"title":"","content":"Well, as I've stated several times on my Monday Meeting Notes, we really don't intend or like to delve into the details on decisions about changes on creative teams. But seriously, do you really think we wanted to make the calls to go back into projects at the stages we have had to and put together whole new teams of writers and developers?<br /> <br /> Our pay rates are not secret and are hardly out of line for the tabletop RPG biz - some companies pay more, and a lot more pay less. Plus, in January we revised, upward, writers' pay per word rates and changed entirely our developer pay methods in order to more fairly compensate our devs for all the work they do. Are these rates what all the talented people truly deserve? No, they are what we can pay and continue publishing in this tiny little corner of the publishing business.<br /> <br /> As for not getting paid- if any freelancer has not been paid, they should contact me right now at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#e99b808a819da99d818c8687909199889d81c78a8684\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"ff8d969c978bbf8b979a909186878f9e8b97d19c9092\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. Seriously, mistakes happen, but I've been getting freelancers paid for 25 years and I'm not going to stop now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:38:51-07:00","id":1077137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077130#post1077130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to distract from this thread, but Shadowrun treats their freelancers pretty fucking awfully; there was a whole embezzling scandal that was never resolved, and the situation with pay was so bad that the Eclipse Phase people bought their own rights back from the main company in order to go independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I can tell, Atlas seems to have a pretty good reputation. I'm also diving into reading Greg Stolze's Reign and Unknown Armies, which are both pretty phenomenal. That latter one has a few familiar WW/OPP freelancers other than Stolze, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:42:05-07:00","id":1077140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077130#post1077130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to distract from this thread, but Shadowrun treats their freelancers pretty fucking awfully; there was a whole embezzling scandal that was never resolved, and the situation with pay was so bad that the Eclipse Phase people bought their own rights back from the main company in order to go independent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then just GURPS for me then. It's the only one you really need anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:45:03-07:00","id":1077141,"title":"","content":"Never was a fan of David Hill. He's a decent writer, but I simply can't stand him as a person, his views on law enforcement, and the way he interacts with people. He writes negatively about the people he works with, throws shade at the company who employs him, finds himself fired, and then wonders why?<br /> <br /> If this happened in just about any occupation, the same thing would occur. He's probably better off going into business for himself.<br /> <br /> I certainly can understand your decision, however, Atamajakki. And I respect it. I'd do the same if I felt strongly about something. Which is why I don't buy Hill's products.<br /> <br /> To me, though? Onyx Path simply puts out too many amazing products by too many quality individuals to let one person's drama sway me from buying their products. I'm sure there's plenty of products that Hill is working on where he'd love your support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 04-12-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:49:54-07:00","id":1077142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077137#post1077137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I can tell, Atlas seems to have a pretty good reputation. I'm also diving into reading Greg Stolze's Reign and Unknown Armies, which are both pretty phenomenal. That latter one has a few familiar WW/OPP freelancers other than Stolze, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolze is a gift. I think I said &quot;he could shoot me in the gut and I'd thank him for it&quot; on my blog the other day. UA3 has been a delight to read so far and has had some surprisingly great trans representation in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077141#post1077141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never was a fan of David Hill. He's a decent writer, but I simply can't stand him as a person, his views on law enforcement, and the way he interacts with people. He writes negatively about the people he works with, throws shade at the company who employs him, finds himself fired, and then wonders why?<br /> <br /> If this happened in just about any occupation, the same thing would occur. He's probably better off going into business for himself.<br /> <br /> I certainly can understand your decision, however, Atamajakki. And I respect it. I'd do the same if I felt strongly about something. Which is why I don't buy Hill's products.<br /> <br /> To me, though? Onyx Path simply puts out too many amazing products by too many quality individuals to let one person's drama sway me from buying their products. I'm sure there's plenty of products that Hill is working on where he'd love your support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suit yourself. He's said nothing I've disagreed with over the years and has consistently put out emotionally important material to me; it would surprise me if Changeling 2e is no longer going to be the amazing survivor allegory it was shaping up to me, and that's a travesty in my eues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:59:55-07:00","id":1077149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077142#post1077142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stolze is a gift. I think I said &quot;he could shoot me in the gut and I'd thank him for it&quot; on my blog the other day. UA3 has been a delight to read so far and has had some surprisingly great trans representation in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Suit yourself. He's said nothing I've disagreed with over the years and has consistently put out emotionally important material to me; it would surprise me if Changeling 2e is no longer going to be the amazing survivor allegory it was shaping up to me, and that's a travesty in my eues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stolze is a fantastic writer, as an aside. There are a number of great writers who've worked for OP/WW in the past that went on to become famous. Chuck Wendig is another one. <br /> <br /> Anyways, I get it Lex. I do. As an athlete, there are a ton of people and companies that I refuse to do business with because of who they are and what they represent. There are 7 billion people on this planet. We're not going to get along with everyone. <br /> <br /> I just hope that after some time, you do find it in your heart to come back to the fold.<br /> <br /> Deviant is looking fantastic, for example. And since I know(think?) you're a huge fan of the CoD, Dark Eras 2 will likely be just as fantastic as Dark Eras 1 is. : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:11:28-07:00","id":1077158,"title":"","content":"Best of luck to you, Lex. I hope you find games you enjoy and have a fun time playing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:11:54-07:00","id":1077159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077136#post1077136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I've stated several times on my Monday Meeting Notes, we really don't intend or like to delve into the details on decisions about changes on creative teams. But seriously, do you really think we wanted to make the calls to go back into projects at the stages we have had to and put together whole new teams of writers and developers?<br /> <br /> Our pay rates are not secret and are hardly out of line for the tabletop RPG biz - some companies pay more, and a lot more pay less. Plus, in January we revised, upward, writers' pay per word rates and changed entirely our developer pay methods in order to more fairly compensate our devs for all the work they do. Are these rates what all the talented people truly deserve? No, they are what we can pay and continue publishing in this tiny little corner of the publishing business.<br /> <br /> As for not getting paid- if any freelancer has not been paid, they should contact me right now at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#691b000a011d291d010c0607101119081d01470a0604\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"14667d777c6054607c717b7a6d6c6475607c3a777b79\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. Seriously, mistakes happen, but I've been getting freelancers paid for 25 years and I'm not going to stop now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this is all a big misunderstanding and that I'm just foolishly getting sucked into a dispute that's none of my business. I want to support companies who treat their people well, and it's disturbing to hear that co-developers are splitting small checks and each making something like $.75 a word as a result. I'm glad to hear that pay has been boosted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:24:03-07:00","id":1077166,"title":"","content":"I think $.75 cents a word would be a lot, especially for 10-30 thousand word entries. Freelancing advice suggests pay is between .10 and 1.00 a word. I have to imagine the 1.00 a word is for much smaller bites or larger industries, like a 1,500 word article in a big periodical. Consumer Reports apparently does between 1 and 1.50 per word, but that's with articles limited to 1,000 words. The Wall Street Journal seems to only pay .50 a word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:28:42-07:00","id":1077173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077166#post1077166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think $.75 cents a word would be a lot, especially for 10-30 thousand word entries. Freelancing advice suggests pay is between .10 and 1.00 a word. I have to imagine the 1.00 a word is for much smaller bites or larger industries, like a 1,500 word article in a big periodical. Consumer Reports apparently does between 1 and 1.50 per word, but that's with articles limited to 1,000 words. The Wall Street Journal seems to only pay .50 a word.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Especially in the RPG industry which is not exactly what one would call &quot;healthy.&quot; Onyx Path is not Marvel/Disney. They have to make business decisions that will enable their company to continue to produce great products and at the same time keep their employees happy. It's not easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:34:38-07:00","id":1077178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077130#post1077130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to distract from this thread, but Shadowrun treats their freelancers pretty fucking awfully; there was a whole embezzling scandal that was never resolved, and the situation with pay was so bad that the Eclipse Phase people bought their own rights back from the main company in order to go independent.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077140#post1077140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then just GURPS for me then. It's the only one you really need anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's just the BTS stuff with Catalyst Game Labs and the Shadowrun brand.<br /> <br /> Then there's the stuff regarding the recent Shadowrun products themselves: putting out rushed, typo-ridden products, errata either taking forever to get pushed if errata even gets considered at all (which it often isn't), terrible communication with customers/fans regarding products' progress and their release, and overall toxic behavior and interactions between said fans and their writers. Then there's the Shadowrun tactical miniatures game and board game that still haven't been released, despite being announced as far back as 2012, but where updates suddenly stopped in 2014 . With the reason given being that they've been unable to secure manufacturing deals to make all the physical materials.<br /> <br /> (...even though CGL is also the current holder of the Battletech license, a game franchise that's exclusively known for being a miniatures game...yeah...)<br /> <br /> ...yeah I left the Shadowrun community for a reason.<br /> <br /> While I don't entirely agree with atamajakki's reasons for leaving, I can sympathize with the sentiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-12-2017, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:05:26-07:00","id":1077204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077136#post1077136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these rates what all the talented people truly deserve? No, they are what we can pay and continue publishing in this tiny little corner of the publishing business.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of us agreed with that when it came to Exalted, the community was pretty happy with the backer levels that would give the writers a bit of a pay boost. However I've heard reports that they never received that bonus, and was kinda curious whether there's any truth to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/315-fluffysquirrel","name":"FluffySquirrel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:12:57-07:00","id":1077208,"title":"","content":"I was disturbed today by the aforementioned twitter conversations which seem to have multiple pretty specific examples of bad behavior. I'm not sure what to say but I find it very disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 04-12-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:32:13-07:00","id":1077228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FluffySquirrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077204#post1077204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a lot of us agreed with that when it came to Exalted, the community was pretty happy with the backer levels that would give the writers a bit of a pay boost. However I've heard reports that they never received that bonus, and was kinda curious whether there's any truth to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs prepare the pay sheets that are sent in, and Holden and I specifically spoke about them including the pay bumps. If that didn't happen, perhaps he should message any one of us about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:33:06-07:00","id":1077230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FluffySquirrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077204#post1077204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a lot of us agreed with that when it came to Exalted, the community was pretty happy with the backer levels that would give the writers a bit of a pay boost. However I've heard reports that they never received that bonus, and was kinda curious whether there's any truth to that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you folks know how pay is processed at Onyx Path?<br /> <br /> (It's rhetorical; if you know, great, if not, read on.)<br /> <br /> Every writer is supposed to have a contract for each project, which details HOW MUCH and WHAT they get paid. For example, let's take my contract for, say, Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised (so this would have been...what, 1999, about? 2000?). At the time, I was making 4 cents a word. I was contracted to writing something like 30,000 words, so I was getting a flat fee of $1200. With me so far? That's the HOW MUCH.<br /> <br /> As for the WHEN, I'm pretty sure that back then my contracts worked on a &quot;50% on final draft, 50% on publication&quot; kind of model (there were a few different models and which one you were on depended on how much work you had done for WW and whether they considered you reliable; WW Rev was only my third project). So I'd get $600 when I turned in my final draft and the other $600 when the book was published.<br /> <br /> Ah, but how would Rebecca (who was White Wolf's accounts payable person) know to pay me? My developer (Ethan Skemp, on this particular project) would send in a PAY SCHEDULE, telling Rebecca HOW MUCH to pay me and WHERE to send it.<br /> <br /> So, nowadays, this process is pretty similar. The pay schedules get sent in a pdf instead of in an email, there's an option to be paid via Paypal, but otherwise, that's how it works.<br /> <br /> Now, as a thought exercise, I want you to go through that process and see if you figure out where it could break down, and who's fault that would be. Go ahead, I'll be here all week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","user":"blackhatmatt","date":". 04-12-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:49:24-07:00","id":1077239,"title":"","content":"Wow I just went through that exchange, kind of hard to get through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13260-hp-dovecraft","name":"HP Dovecraft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:02:45-07:00","id":1077248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077230#post1077230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as a thought exercise, I want you to go through that process and see if you figure out where it could break down, and who's fault that would be. Go ahead, I'll be here all week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm parsing this. Are you suggesting that in some way Holden was responsible by not asking for payment correctly? Not only do I find that difficult to believe, it seems to ignore the fact that several individuals on the twitter spoke of having very similar issues. Are they all failing to fill out pay schedules properly, I suppose, is the implication?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:05:26-07:00","id":1077250,"title":"","content":"Not to derail the thread too much but I've always been curious as to the breakdown of funds from a kickstarter. How does a quarter to half a million dollar pie get sliced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:09:46-07:00","id":1077255,"title":"","content":"We outside the conversation on Twitter and elsewhere are witnesses to only one side of a grievance. The other side is maintaining confidentiality about the entire thing. We can have a decent degree of faith that Onyx Path wouldn't have removed a contracted developer without a good reason. It's pointless to spout conjecture when you're only ever going to see one side of this episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:17:27-07:00","id":1077262,"title":"","content":"So your saying they are breaching some sort of nda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:19:20-07:00","id":1077266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077262#post1077262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your saying they are breaching some sort of nda?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. I'm saying one person says they were wronged, and the other party is keeping its reasons for that individual's dismissal private, as most responsible employers would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:38:35-07:00","id":1077287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077266#post1077266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. I'm saying one person says they were wronged, and the other party is keeping its reasons for that individual's dismissal private, as most responsible employers would.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, David left of his own volition.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's still understandable that Onyx Path would want to keep private their side of the story, but this isn't exactly a termination of employment so much as David quitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:42:08-07:00","id":1077290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077287#post1077287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, David left of his own volition.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's still understandable that Onyx Path would want to keep private their side of the story, but this isn't exactly a termination of employment so much as David quitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you understand it, yes. But according to David in his most recent Facebook post, OPP had a new developer lined up for several months, and was indeed keeping the project in development despite the developer being finished with the project and having his final draft turned in.<br /> <br /> In other words, OPP had terminated him months before his actual leave, or must have somehow been planning for him to leave months in advance. David had zero intention of leaving until they hired his stalker Zak S, and left OPP because WW hired his stalker Zak S. He left because of Zak S. It was a sudden kind of thing, not a thing talked over for months.<br /> <br /> That's the controversy.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, since I have yet to comment in thread otherwise, here are my thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) some shady shit up in this thing<br /> <br /> 2) I will go on missing AtamajakkI forever, it seems.<br /> <br /> 3) I am deeply concerned about all of this and will be keeping my eye on it, but I've already decided I'm supporting OPP so I'm already trash and not going to change my mind over a dev (even my favorite dev) getting fired. I've already done the &quot;leave dirt bag company to support brave independent dev&quot; thing before and got burned by it, hard. I'm just gonna keep supporting companies and independent devs alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","user":"RomulusGloriosus","date":". 04-12-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:49:21-07:00","id":1077297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077266#post1077266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. I'm saying one person says they were wronged, and the other party is keeping its reasons for that individual's dismissal private, as most responsible employers would.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This 10000%<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:00:36-07:00","id":1077308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077248#post1077248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I'm parsing this. Are you suggesting that in some way Holden was responsible by not asking for payment correctly? Not only do I find that difficult to believe, it seems to ignore the fact that several individuals on the twitter spoke of having very similar issues. Are they all failing to fill out pay schedules properly, I suppose, is the implication?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not suggesting anything. I'm asking you (general you) to consider where, in that scenario, the problems could arise.<br /> <br /> But since you brought it up...<br /> <br /> Let's say a developer (I'm not singling anyone out here, because generally I'm only privy to what developers do when they're <i>me</i> or when I'm working for them) is derelict in their duties and doesn't fill out the pay schedule. You could legitimately argue that OPP bears at least some of the responsibility because ultimately the buck stops with them, but I think it's also fair to argue that the dev bears some of the responsibility because part of their job, as developer, is handling that end of things (filing pay schedules fall under the &quot;wrangling authors&quot; side of things). <br /> <br /> But if a dev did not perform that part of their duties, whether by omission or deliberately, and then went around complaining that authors had not been paid despite <i>their part</i> in authors not being paid, what would you call that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:08:02-07:00","id":1077314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077308#post1077308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if a dev did not perform that part of their duties, whether by omission or deliberately, and then went around complaining that authors had not been paid despite <i>their part</i> in authors not being paid, what would you call that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that encapsulates why I'm not understanding your point here - did you read the twitter thread? The complaints aren't only coming from one developer and the authors underneath them that are supposed to be wrangled. They are coming from multiple game lines. So this implication just doesn't make sense, or maybe it's just going over my head completely. If so and I've misunderstood, please explain!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:29:51-07:00","id":1077327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077314#post1077314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that encapsulates why I'm not understanding your point here - did you read the twitter thread? The complaints aren't only coming from one developer and the authors underneath them that are supposed to be wrangled. They are coming from multiple game lines. So this implication just doesn't make sense, or maybe it's just going over my head completely. If so and I've misunderstood, please explain!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who wishes dearly that social media(Twitter, Facebook, and Tumblr specifically) died a horrible death, what is THE thread on twitter that is saying this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:57:12-07:00","id":1077339,"title":"","content":"I believe they were referring to this thread. at least, this was the one that was linked earlier in the day:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/HoldenShearer/status/848203921713762304\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1597876803/HamtaroLarge_400x400.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/HoldenShearer/status/848203921713762304\" target=\"_blank\"> Holden Shearer (@HoldenShearer) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/HoldenShearer/status/848203921713762304\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mobile.twitter.com/HoldenShearer/status/848203921713762304 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> OPP unfollowed me on twitter. harsh D= </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13260-hp-dovecraft","name":"HP Dovecraft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:40:08-07:00","id":1077391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077314#post1077314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that encapsulates why I'm not understanding your point here - did you read the twitter thread? The complaints aren't only coming from one developer and the authors underneath them that are supposed to be wrangled. They are coming from multiple game lines. So this implication just doesn't make sense, or maybe it's just going over my head completely. If so and I've misunderstood, please explain!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, Twitter. <br /> <br /> So, couple of things about that thread that I think are pertinent (and if I'm wrong about any of this, perhaps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> will be good enough to correct me). <br /> <br /> <b>Exalted 3rd</b> started when WW and the associated games were still owned by CCP. Things (contractually) were different then, and continued to change all the way through. I do not know what the particulars of Holden's contract with CCP/WW/OPP were, so I can't speak to that. <br /> <br /> Reading over that thread, I'm seeing a lot of claims from David that, at the very least, need further context. Jeez, where to start. <br /> <br /> It was the case as recently as <b>Promethean 2nd Edition</b> (which, while it was just published, was actually contracted in 2014) that OPP provided a comp copy to authors (hell, back in the day, we got three, but that was when White Wolf was doing actual print runs rather than POD, which changes the metric somewhat). Nowadays, our contracts give us a free digital copy and the option to buy a POD at cost. I usually buy the books I work on because I like having a physical copy, and I've never had any trouble getting codes to do so. When Holden and David talk about having trouble chasing down their physical copies, I have to wonder where the problem is happening (like, I'm not being sarcastic - my experience has been that it's really easy, so I'm not sure where the disconnect is). With that said, I'm firmly of the opinion that OPP should provide freelancers with at least one physical comp. I've said as much to Rich. <br /> <br /> David mentions something about <b>contracts being changed after the fact</b>, <b>being paid less than what he was contracted for</b>, and <b>contracts moving from a flat rate (prescribed word count x word rate) to some other system based on...words actually published?</b> I have no idea what he's talking about. Every contract I've ever taken on for White Wolf, when they were independent, owned by CCP, and owned by OPP, has been paid. There have occasionally been delays in payment, but almost universally, those delays were because a developer didn't file a pay schedule on time or properly (note that I did say &quot;almost&quot;; there have been delays on the administrative end, too. They have not, however, been anything like a consistent problem). <br /> <br /> Oh, and? When people are working for me as a dev, they know (or should know) that I'll go to bat for them if they don't get paid, if they don't get comps, or if something's not right...but only if they <i>tell me. </i><br /> <br /> For reference, I started freelancing for OPP in 1997, and I've lost count of the number of contracts I've fulfilled for them. So, again, if there's a problem, it's not universal, so you have to ask where the problem is and why. <br /> <br /> What else (again, man, fuck Twitter; it's hard to parse). Ok, Wood talks a little about<b> word rates</b>. It <i>is</i> true that up until a few years go (around the time of the CCP merger I <i>think</i>, but I couldn't put a date on it so don't ask me to), White Wolf paid 6 cents a word as their highest regular rate (though you'd occasionally find higher ones for individual projects under weird circumstances; I got 10 cents a word once because I turned in 4000 words overnight, last minute). I was making 6 cents a word for a while. Then, WW lowered that ceiling to 5 cents, which affected me and maybe a half-dozen other people (at most).<br /> <br /> And I'll be honest, that stung. It felt like my contributions weren't valued. I'd literally never missed a deadline, I'd picked up I don't know how many contracts after other authors dropped out, and I'd consistently been able to bring my books as a dev in on time and (though this is subjective, so take it for what it's worth), well. I strongly considered saying &quot;yeah, screw you guys&quot;, chasing other work, and denouncing OPP. <br /> <br /> I didn't, for a number of reasons. I liked the work I was doing. I knew the people and the IP involved, and getting into something else would have been a learning curve. I was (if my timing's right) in grad school or just out, coping with being a new dad and a new SLP, and putting in the time to learn new games and new IP was too steep for me. Plus, I was <i>there</i> in 2003 when the decision to end the CWoD happened, and I knew what shaky ground everything was on. I decided to give it a go. <br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry to make that all personal, but all of this to say: It's not unheard of for OPP to change procedures or numbers. They have never, to my knowledge, changed a contract once it's been signed. Usually, it's a &quot;going forward, here's the deal&quot; thing. So, again, if what David's saying is true, none of the recent books I've signed contracts for reflect it. <br /> <br /> OK, this has gotten too freaking long already and I'm not gonna pick through that whole thread. Tell you what: You want to know about something, link the tweet, hit me on FB, email me, PM me, or just ask me some specific. Unless it's confidentiality that's not mine to breach, I'll tell you, if I know. <br /> <br /> Sunshine is the best disinfectant, and I don't have anything to lose, here. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:09:05-07:00","id":1077413,"title":"","content":"I thought that David had better...I don't know, everything about this is in poor taste. Well, I hope everything will end up changing for the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:27:58-07:00","id":1077429,"title":"","content":"Thank you Matt for your detailed explanations.<br /> <br /> I really just can't be too angry at the roleplaying industry and the way it pays its freelancers. Writing books is hard work, but it's a very weak industry that's really only hanging on for dear life outside of Wizards of the Coast, and they get most of their money off Magic: The Gathering anyhow. This isn't some super conglomerate not valuing their employees and paying them shit, it's one dude desperately trying to keep a dying industry alive out of love for the intellectual property who is (possibly??) doing some shady shit because the Business World is a steaming load of crap and this industry probably shouldn't still be alive in this market and you've got to do what you've got to do to keep it going for as long as you can.<br /> <br /> Yes, the whole industry could just devolve into individual independent game developers developing their own games and making wholesale exactly what they put in, and I wouldn't object to that, but once there's no more 'big game company' keeping you on a deadline, you get lazy and stop doing it because development is hard and it doesn't pay enough.<br /> <br /> As I said, I've been burned by indie devs too strong to do anything more than just support them when they release stuff, and ignore them when they don't. No more loyalty pledges from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:43:05-07:00","id":1077441,"title":"","content":"I don't like &quot;indie&quot; games usually, so well. I hope that &quot;indie&quot; current that seemed to infect OPP lately (maybe I'm wrong and biased, but It somehow always seemed to gather around David's things) will stop, honestly. Less Hurt Lockers, more Vampire the Requiems, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:59:04-07:00","id":1077453,"title":"","content":"It's a shame that things have progressed the way they did, but please keep in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) that this is an industry founded by, aimed at, and still run by intelligent, opinionated people.<br /> 2) Sometimes those opinions clash and tempers flare. As with any other business, the employee yelling 'screw you, I'm out' is much more free to make a scene than the employer.<br /> 3) Twitter and other social media make it far too easy to go on one sided rants, and people sometimes forget that 'burning bridges' isn't usually the best way to go out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:11:04-07:00","id":1077463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077441#post1077441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less Hurt Lockers, more Vampire the Requiems, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you unpack that a bit? I'm not sure what quality you are attributing to indie-ness that Hurt Locker had and Requiem didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:25:07-07:00","id":1077471,"title":"","content":"Vampire is very streamlined and consistent in quality. It's a well oiled game with good ideas backed up by solid, consistent mechanics. Writing emphasises mechanics, mechanics emphasize themes emphasize writing. It all works in sync. And I'm saying this as someone who is not a vampire fan; I don't like vampire as a &quot;genre&quot;, I'm not a fan of vampire media.<br /> A lot of my problems with certain elements in certain books is that they have quite good ideas, but their execution - especially mechanical - is inconsistent and often look like they have potential...but also need like 10 extra rewrites and reworks to make them actually quality work. The most polite way to say it would be, I guess, it's unpolished? &quot;Great idea, not worked and thought through enough&quot;, with a book trying to tell me &quot;but that's ok, just figure something out and fix it on your own, it's not my job to provide you with a working stuff, just to inspire you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T20:51:23-07:00","id":1077485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077471#post1077471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is very streamlined and consistent in quality. It's a well oiled game with good ideas backed up by solid, consistent mechanics. Writing emphasises mechanics, mechanics emphasize themes emphasize writing. It all works in sync. And I'm saying this as someone who is not a vampire fan; I don't like vampire as a &amp;quot;genre&amp;quot;, I'm not a fan of vampire media.<br /> A lot of my problems with certain elements in certain books is that they have quite good ideas, but their execution - especially mechanical - is inconsistent and often look like they have potential...but also need like 10 extra rewrites and reworks to make them actually quality work. The most polite way to say it would be, I guess, it's unpolished? &amp;quot;Great idea, not worked and thought through enough&amp;quot;, with a book trying to tell me &amp;quot;but that's ok, just figure something out and fix it on your own, it's not my job to provide you with a working stuff, just to inspire you&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I gotcha. Thanks for elaborating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:58:02-07:00","id":1077667,"title":"","content":"If you want me to elaborate, or want to share your thoughts, you can always hit me up on PM. I'm not as vicious as some people paint me up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:59:28-07:00","id":1077781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077453#post1077453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>2) Sometimes those opinions clash and tempers flare. As with any other business, the employee yelling 'screw you, I'm out' is much more free to make a scene than the employer.<br /> 3) Twitter and other social media make it far too easy to go on one sided rants, and people sometimes forget that 'burning bridges' isn't usually the best way to go out.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So much yes in this post, but numbers 2 and 3 especially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:40:10-07:00","id":1077790,"title":"","content":"All this reminds me why i generally don't focus on the person of creators, but on the products I like. I want to enjoy nice things without the added personal drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T10:53:45-07:00","id":1077797,"title":"","content":"Prolly not worth it. I don't have a dog in this race. <br /> <br /> There is a perception that David chose to leave due to OPP mistreating him in retaliation over of his complaints about Zak S. I doubt that's true, but it might behoove OPP to make it clear that it wasn't the case. I've seen people suggesting as much on other corners of the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-13-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T11:21:58-07:00","id":1077812,"title":"","content":"But...David left on his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:40:26-07:00","id":1077855,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was David's choice to stop developing for Onyx Path. He was freelance after all, not an employee, so they couldn't exactly fire him, only stop offering him gigs. And it would be silly to assume that the license holders of (some of) OPP's products hiring his abuser didn't have <i>something</i> to do with his decision to leave, but if his social media indicates one thing it's that he was unhappy with Onyx Path for more reasons than that, and it would be equally silly to assume it was the only reason he left. Most likely that was just the proverbial straw. As people have been pointing out though, Onyx Path doesn't really have the luxury of being able to trash talk David as he does them. There's a side of this we're not seeing. As I have a lot of respect for both parties, this feels like watching friends who have been dating for a long time go through a rough breakup. I don't want to take sides because I care a lot for both of them, so the best I can do is assume there were good and bad reasons on both sides, and to try to support each as best I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:05:04-07:00","id":1077867,"title":"","content":"Sigh, this whole affair has been a big unfortunate reminder of why I don't participate with the Exalted community anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 04-13-2017, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:15:39-07:00","id":1077918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1077105-i-m-done?p=1077855#post1077855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't want to take sides because I care a lot for both of them, so the best I can do is assume there were good and bad reasons on both sides, and to try to support each as best I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>To that end, I recently bought and have been enjoying <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/147795/Apotheosis-Drive-X--FatePowered-Mecha-RPG--HD-Mix?term=apotheosis+drive&amp;test_epoch=0\" target=\"_blank\">Apotheosis Drive X</a>, a Mecha RPG in the vein of Gundam from Dave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link